Networking: SDD

Purpose:
  Define networking principles, CDN, load balancer, API gateway,
  DNS, TLS, and network security rules.

Principles:
  All external traffic MUST be encrypted with TLS.
  Network security MUST follow zero-trust principles.
  Firewall rules MUST be deny-by-default.
  DNS MUST use low TTL for failover-capable records.
  All inter-service communication MUST use DNS names, never IPs.

CDN:
  description: Content Delivery Network for static assets and API caching
  when_to_use: L1+, static assets, global user base, DDoS protection
  configuration:
    cache_rules: immutable assets 1 year TTL, HTML no cache,
                 API responses respect Cache-Control
    origin_security: origin MUST allow only CDN IP ranges

LoadBalancer:
  types:
    L4: transport layer (TCP/UDP)
    L7: application layer (HTTP/HTTPS)
  algorithms: round-robin, least-connections, weighted, ip-hash
  health_checks: active periodic probe, passive error monitoring
  high_availability: deploy at least 2 load balancers

APIGateway:
  description: Entry point for external API traffic
  responsibilities: routing, authentication, rate limiting, transformation
  when_to_use: external API exposure, multiple client types, L2+
  rule: gateway MUST handle only cross-cutting concerns

DNS:
  internal: service discovery, TTL 60s for dynamic services
  external: low TTL (300s) for failover, geographic DNS for multi-region
  anti_patterns:
    hardcoded_ips: MUST use DNS names
    long_ttl: critical services MUST have TTL <= 60s

TLS:
  external_traffic: HTTPS mandatory, TLS 1.3 minimum, strong ciphers
  internal_traffic: mTLS for service mesh, TLS for sensitive APIs
  certificate_management: managed service, automated renewal

NetworkSecurity:
  zero_trust: authenticate every request, authorize minimum access,
              encrypt all traffic, inspect all traffic, log all access
  segmentation: separate networks by sensitivity, private subnets for internal
  DDoS: CDN absorption, rate limiting at edge, traffic scrubbing

FirewallRules:
  principles:
    deny_by_default: default deny all inbound, explicit allow required
    least_privilege: allow only required ports and source IPs
    outbound: restrict to required destinations, monitor unexpected traffic
  configuration: rules MUST be version controlled and audited

AntiPatterns:
  OpenFirewall: MUST deny by default, allow explicitly
  UnencryptedInternal: sensitive internal traffic MUST be encrypted
  IPHardcoding: MUST use DNS names with TTL
  SingleRegion: L99.95+ MUST span regions
  MonitoringBlindSpots: internal traffic MUST be monitored

